Per-directory terms
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  /            MIT License                          LICENSE
  compiler/    Apache License 2.0                   compiler/LICENSE
               with LLVM Exception

Everything published through the four release channels — the GitHub Action, the
VS Code extension, the Open VSX listing and the Chrome extension — is built from
the MIT-licensed part of the tree. compiler/ is outside the npm workspaces and is
not part of any of those artifacts.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why compiler/ carries different terms
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

compiler/ builds against the Clang and LLVM development headers and links against
LLVM libraries. LLVM is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 with LLVM
Exception. Matching those terms for the directory that compiles against them
keeps the combination unambiguous, and it is the licence upstream chose precisely
so that the result of linking against LLVM can be redistributed without imposing
additional obligations on the linked work.

No LLVM source is copied into this repository. compiler/ includes LLVM headers
from a locally installed toolchain at build time; the headers and libraries stay
where the system package manager put them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Runtime and build dependencies are declared in package.json files and resolved
from the npm registry; their licences are those stated by their publishers and
are reproduced in the installed node_modules tree rather than here.

LLVM/Clang (https://llvm.org/) — Apache License 2.0 with LLVM Exception.
Used as a build-time and link-time dependency of compiler/ only.
